msgid "Leverage trim SQD for improved configuration selection for the latest version of Sample-based quantum diagonalization (SQD)"
msgstr "Manfaatkan trim SQD untuk pemilihan konfigurasi yang lebih baik untuk versi terbaru Sample-based quantum diagonalization (SQD)"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Leverage trim SQD for improved configuration selection"
msgstr "Manfaatkan trim SQD untuk pemilihan konfigurasi yang lebih baik"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<OpenInLabBanner notebookPath=\"addons/qiskit-addon-sqd/guides/trim-sqd.ipynb\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The default behavior of [`diagonalize_fermionic_hamiltonian`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-addon-sqd/fermion) is to diagonalize each subsampled batch and keep the best result. **Trim SQD** instead treats the batches as candidates to be screened: each is diagonalized, *trimmed* down to the configurations carrying the largest weight, and the survivors of all the batches are merged and diagonalized together. That merged diagonalization is the one whose energy the iteration reports, and its own trimmed output seeds the next iteration.\n"
msgstr "Perilaku default [`diagonalize_fermionic_hamiltonian`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-addon-sqd/fermion) adalah mendiagonalisasi setiap batch hasil subsampling dan menyimpan hasil terbaik. **Trim SQD** sebaliknya memperlakukan batch sebagai kandidat yang disaring: masing-masing didiagonalisasi, di-*trim* hingga tersisa konfigurasi dengan bobot terbesar, lalu sisa dari semua batch digabung dan didiagonalisasi bersama. Diagonalisasi gabungan itulah yang energinya dilaporkan oleh iterasi, dan output hasil trim-nya menjadi benih untuk iterasi berikutnya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The trim SQD implementation is based on joint research from\n"
"the Cleveland Clinic Foundation, RIKEN, and IBM&reg;. If you use this feature in\n"
"your research, also cite the paper. You can find the citation in the\n"
"`CITATION.bib` file, with citation key `merz2026crossing`.\n"
msgstr ""
"Implementasi trim SQD didasarkan pada riset bersama dari\n"
"Cleveland Clinic Foundation, RIKEN, dan IBM&reg;. Jika kamu memakai fitur ini dalam\n"
"riset kamu, kutip juga makalahnya. Kutipannya ada di berkas\n"
"`CITATION.bib`, dengan citation key `merz2026crossing`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For more details on the SQD code used in this example, see the [chemistry Hamiltonian tutorial](/tutorials/sample-based-quantum-diagonalization).\n"
msgstr "Untuk detail lebih lanjut tentang kode SQD yang dipakai di contoh ini, lihat [tutorial Hamiltonian kimia](/tutorials/sample-based-quantum-diagonalization).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Set up the molecule {#set-up-the-molecule}"
msgstr "Siapkan molekulnya {#set-up-the-molecule}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Run the loop {#run-the-loop}"
msgstr "Jalankan loop-nya {#run-the-loop}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "One trim SQD iteration does the following:\n"
msgstr "Satu iterasi trim SQD melakukan hal berikut:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Screening round.** Partition the bitstrings into batches.  Diagonalize each batch and keep the `trim_ratio` fraction of its CI strings, per spin sector, ranked by weight.\n"
msgstr "**Putaran penyaringan.** Bagi bitstring menjadi batch.  Diagonalisasi setiap batch dan simpan sebagian `trim_ratio` dari string CI-nya, per sektor spin, berdasarkan peringkat bobot.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Merged round.** Diagonalize the merged survivors once. This is the result the iteration reports, and its own trimmed strings seed the next iteration.\n"
msgstr "**Putaran gabungan.** Diagonalisasi sisa gabungan itu sekali. Ini adalah hasil yang dilaporkan iterasi, dan string hasil trim-nya menjadi benih untuk iterasi berikutnya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The loop's `sci_solver` performs both rounds, and defaults to this package's PySCF solver.\n"
msgstr "`sci_solver` milik loop menjalankan kedua putaran, dan secara default memakai solver PySCF dari paket ini.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Enable trim SQD by passing the `TrimPolicy` as follows:\n"
msgstr "Aktifkan trim SQD dengan memberikan `TrimPolicy` seperti berikut:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Check whether screening is helping {#check-whether-screening-is-helping}"
msgstr "Periksa apakah penyaringan membantu {#check-whether-screening-is-helping}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Screening has the most to offer when the sampled configurations greatly outnumber what can be diagonalized at once, so that ranking a larger pool genuinely finds configurations a single batch would have missed. It has the least to offer when a subspace of the affordable size already captures most of the wavefunction.\n"
msgstr "Penyaringan paling bermanfaat saat konfigurasi yang disampel jauh lebih banyak daripada yang bisa didiagonalisasi sekaligus, sehingga meranking kumpulan yang lebih besar benar-benar menemukan konfigurasi yang akan terlewat oleh satu batch. Manfaatnya paling kecil saat subruang dengan ukuran yang terjangkau sudah menangkap sebagian besar fungsi gelombang.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Screening depends on the batches differing from one another. `TrimPolicy` manages this by modifying the behavior of `diagonalize_fermionic_hamiltonian` to draw one pool of `samples_per_batch * num_batches` bitstrings and partitioning it among the batches, so no bitstring appears in more than one.\n"
msgstr "Penyaringan bergantung pada batch yang berbeda satu sama lain. `TrimPolicy` mengelola ini dengan mengubah perilaku `diagonalize_fermionic_hamiltonian` agar menarik satu kumpulan berisi `samples_per_batch * num_batches` bitstring dan membaginya ke antar batch, sehingga tidak ada bitstring yang muncul di lebih dari satu batch.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Bound the subspace {#bound-the-subspace}"
msgstr "Batasi subruangnya {#bound-the-subspace}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A subspace here is spanned by the *Cartesian product* of a spin-alpha and a spin-beta CI string array.\n"
msgstr "Subruang di sini direntang oleh *hasil kali Kartesius* dari array string CI spin-alpha dan spin-beta.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Trimming ranks configurations, but the carryover is two per-spin string lists. Keeping the 150 highest-weight configurations of a subspace typically involves close to 150 distinct alpha strings and 150 distinct beta strings, whose product spans roughly 22,500 configurations, not 150. So the subspace handed to the next iteration is generally much larger than the set that was ranked, and it grows quadratically in what you retain.\n"
msgstr "Trimming meranking konfigurasi, tetapi yang dibawa ke iterasi berikutnya adalah dua daftar string per spin. Mempertahankan 150 konfigurasi berbobot tertinggi dari sebuah subruang biasanya melibatkan sekitar 150 string alpha yang berbeda dan 150 string beta yang berbeda, yang hasil kalinya merentang sekitar 22.500 konfigurasi, bukan 150. Jadi subruang yang diteruskan ke iterasi berikutnya umumnya jauh lebih besar daripada himpunan yang diranking, dan tumbuh secara kuadratik terhadap jumlah yang kamu pertahankan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Trimming and carrying over are bounded separately, because they happen at different points: trimming shrinks each batch of the screening round, while the carryover is what crosses into the next iteration.\n"
msgstr "Trimming dan carryover dibatasi secara terpisah, karena keduanya terjadi di titik yang berbeda: trimming mengecilkan setiap batch pada putaran penyaringan, sedangkan carryover adalah yang berpindah ke iterasi berikutnya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Four arguments bound it, and it is useful to set at least one:\n"
msgstr "Ada empat argumen yang membatasinya, dan sebaiknya atur setidaknya satu:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**`trim_ratio`** is the fraction of each batch's strings, per spin sector, that survive screening. Lower values shrink the merged subspace but discard configurations the next iteration must rediscover by sampling.\n"
msgstr "**`trim_ratio`** adalah fraksi string setiap batch, per sektor spin, yang lolos penyaringan. Nilai yang lebih rendah mengecilkan subruang gabungan tetapi membuang konfigurasi yang harus ditemukan ulang lewat sampling oleh iterasi berikutnya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**`max_strings_per_trim`** caps the strings each batch contributes, per sector, regardless of the ratio. Useful with `symmetrize_spin`, which merges both spin sectors into one list and so roughly doubles what each batch offers. This bound is **per batch**: the merged subspace can hold up to `num_batches` times as many strings, less whatever the batches had in common, which in practice is not much.\n"
msgstr "**`max_strings_per_trim`** membatasi jumlah string yang disumbangkan setiap batch, per sektor, apa pun rasionya. Berguna bersama `symmetrize_spin`, yang menggabungkan kedua sektor spin ke dalam satu daftar sehingga kira-kira menggandakan apa yang ditawarkan setiap batch. Batas ini berlaku **per batch**: subruang gabungan bisa memuat hingga `num_batches` kali lipat string, dikurangi apa pun yang sama antar batch, yang dalam praktiknya tidak banyak.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**`carryover_threshold`**, **`carryover_ratio`**, and **`max_carryover`** bound the strings that seed the next iteration, applied to the merged subspace as a whole rather than per batch. `carryover_threshold` is the amplitude cutoff that `StandardPolicy` uses, with the same default; the other two bound the count, which the cutoff alone does not.\n"
msgstr "**`carryover_threshold`**, **`carryover_ratio`**, dan **`max_carryover`** membatasi string yang menjadi benih iterasi berikutnya, diterapkan ke subruang gabungan secara keseluruhan, bukan per batch. `carryover_threshold` adalah batas amplitudo yang dipakai `StandardPolicy`, dengan nilai default yang sama; dua lainnya membatasi jumlahnya, yang tidak bisa dicapai oleh batas amplitudo saja.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**`max_dim`**, on `diagonalize_fermionic_hamiltonian` itself, bounds each spin sector of every subspace the loop diagonalizes, including the merged one. It acts as a backstop and applies to whatever the policy returns, after the carryover is merged with fresh samples.\n"
msgstr "**`max_dim`**, pada `diagonalize_fermionic_hamiltonian` itu sendiri, membatasi setiap sektor spin dari setiap subruang yang didiagonalisasi loop, termasuk yang gabungan. Ini bertindak sebagai pengaman cadangan dan berlaku untuk apa pun yang dikembalikan policy, setelah carryover digabung dengan sampel baru.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The run above sets `max_strings_per_trim=250` and `max_dim=250` together, so neither what each batch contributes nor the subspace built from it can run away.\n"
msgstr "Run di atas menetapkan `max_strings_per_trim=250` dan `max_dim=250` sekaligus, sehingga baik kontribusi setiap batch maupun subruang yang dibangun darinya tidak bisa membengkak tak terkendali.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use an external eigensolver {#use-an-external-eigensolver}"
msgstr "Pakai eigensolver eksternal {#use-an-external-eigensolver}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "You can use trim SQD with an external eigensolver by passing the `sci_solver` argument:\n"
msgstr "Kamu bisa memakai trim SQD dengan eigensolver eksternal dengan memberikan argumen `sci_solver`:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The prior snippet requires the `sbd-eigensolver` package to be installed from PyPI.\n"
msgstr "Snippet sebelumnya mengharuskan paket `sbd-eigensolver` terpasang dari PyPI.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Distribute the work {#distribute-the-work}"
msgstr "Distribusikan pekerjaannya {#distribute-the-work}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "With `TrimPolicy`, the loop calls `sci_solver` twice per iteration: once with all the batches, and once with the merged subspace. Both calls go through the ordinary `sci_solver` interface, which [this package's multi-process support](/addons/qiskit-addon-sqd/guides/hpc-acceleration) invokes collectively on every MPI rank.\n"
msgstr "Dengan `TrimPolicy`, loop memanggil `sci_solver` dua kali per iterasi: sekali dengan semua batch, dan sekali dengan subruang gabungan. Kedua panggilan lewat antarmuka `sci_solver` biasa, yang dipanggil secara kolektif di setiap rank MPI oleh [dukungan multi-proses paket ini](/addons/qiskit-addon-sqd/guides/hpc-acceleration).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Two levels of parallelism are potentially available, and they are independent:\n"
msgstr "Ada dua tingkat paralelisme yang mungkin tersedia, dan keduanya independen:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Within a diagonalization.** A solver such as SBD can spread a single diagonalization across ranks.\n"
msgstr "**Dalam satu diagonalisasi.** Solver seperti SBD bisa menyebar satu diagonalisasi ke beberapa rank.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Across the batches.** A solver could, in principle, diagonalize the batches concurrently.\n"
msgstr "**Antar batch.** Sebuah solver, pada prinsipnya, bisa mendiagonalisasi batch secara bersamaan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Given a set of batches, the solver determines how to delegate work to its worker processes.\n"
msgstr "Diberi sekumpulan batch, solver menentukan cara mendelegasikan pekerjaan ke proses worker-nya.\n"
